+{"v":1,"seq":521,"channel":"control","type":"message.final","session_id":"replay_session","turn_id":"fixture-turn-1","message_id":"msg_05253661ee4744cb0169815e025f44819e8ffbfa139ac805dd","content":"This is the ctx monorepo: an Agentic Development Environment (ADE) that runs a local daemon to orchestrate coding agents over real workspaces, plus multiple clients and adapters. It’s built around a vendor‑neutral control plane for tasks, sessions, runs/turns, and structured context (ctx Packs), with support for different agent harnesses (Codex/Claude/Gemini/etc.) via adapters.\n\nKey areas you’ll see:\n- `core/` — main product code (daemon + clients + shared packages).\n- `harness-adapters/` and `external-harnesses/` — provider adapters and integrations.\n- `.ctx/ctx-pack/specs/` — the canonical specs that define domain model, APIs, UX invariants, etc.\n- `supabase/` — backend services for subscriptions/entitlements.\n- `docs/`, `partner-docs/`, `prior-art-analyses/` — supporting documentation and research."}
